# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same values on the host.
# Nothing here is required to build or to run the site.

# Where an enquiry from /contact is delivered.
#
# Any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST will do — a form service, an automation
# step, or your own handler. Deliberately provider-agnostic: switching provider
# is a change of this value, not a change of code, and there is no SDK to keep
# up to date. Nothing paid is required.
#
# The POST body is:
#   { subject, name, phone, email, town, message, receivedAt }
#
# Setting this is not enough on its own. Send a real enquiry through the live
# form, watch it arrive in the inbox somebody actually reads, and only then set
# DELIVERY_CONFIGURED to true in src/lib/enquiry.ts. Until that flag is on, the
# form is not rendered and /contact gives the phone number and the email address
# instead — which is the right behaviour, not a placeholder.
ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=
